\pard\b\fs24 1. Overview\b0\par
Editor Navigator is a Unity Editor tool that adds keyboard-first workflows to the Unity Editor. It lets you reorganize objects in the Hierarchy window and move assets in the Project window without dragging and dropping.\par
Key features:\par
\pard\li360\sa120\sl276\slmult1
{\pntext\f1\'b7} Move Hierarchy objects up or down by sibling index.\par
{\pntext\f1\'b7} Reparent objects (Move In) and unparent objects (Move Out).\par
{\pntext\f1\'b7} Project Move Mode with a highlighted target folder.\par
{\pntext\f1\'b7} Multi-selection support.\par
{\pntext\f1\'b7} Undo support for all Hierarchy operations.\par
{\pntext\f1\'b7} A built-in Settings and Help window with a shortcut reference.\par
\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
\pard\b\fs24 2. Requirements\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa120\sl276\slmult1
{\pntext\f1\'b7} Unity 2021.3 or later.\par
{\pntext\f1\'b7} Editor-only package; no runtime components and no third-party dependencies.\par
\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
\pard\b\fs24 3. Installation\b0\par
Follow these steps to install the package in your project.\par
\pard\li360\sa120\sl276\slmult1
Step 1. Open the Unity Editor and open your project.\par
Step 2. In the Project window, navigate to the Assets folder.\par
Step 3. Copy the {\i com.gigaduck.editor-navigator} folder into your project's Assets folder. If you installed from the Asset Store, the package is already imported and you can skip to Step 5.\par
Step 4. Allow Unity to import the package. A short compilation will run; wait until the Editor finishes importing.\par
Step 5. Verify the installation. In the main menu, open {\i Tools} > {\i Hierarchy Navigator} > {\i Settings && Help}. If the window opens, the package is installed correctly.\par
\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
\pard\b\fs24 4. Quick Start\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa120\sl276\slmult1
Step 1. Open a scene in your project.\par
Step 2. In the Hierarchy window, select one or more objects.\par
Step 3. Press Ctrl+Shift+Up or Ctrl+Shift+Down to move the selected objects up or down.\par
Step 4. Press Ctrl+Shift+Right to parent the selected objects under the sibling directly above them.\par
Step 5. Press Ctrl+Shift+Left to unparent the selected objects.\par
Step 6. To move assets: select files in the Project window, press Ctrl+Shift+Up or Ctrl+Shift+Down to enter Move Mode, browse folders with the arrow keys, then press Enter to confirm or Esc to cancel.\par
\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
\pard\b\fs24 5. Usage Guide\b0\par
\pard\b\fs22 5.1 Hierarchy Shortcuts\b0\par
The following shortcuts work while the Hierarchy window is focused. All operations support Undo (Ctrl+Z) and multi-selection.\par
\pard\li360\sa120\sl276\slmult1
{\pntext\f1\'b7} Ctrl+Shift+Up: Move selected object(s) up one sibling.\par
{\pntext\f1\'b7} Ctrl+Shift+Down: Move selected object(s) down one sibling.\par
{\pntext\f1\'b7} Ctrl+Shift+Right: Parent selected object(s) under the sibling above (Move In).\par
{\pntext\f1\'b7} Ctrl+Shift+Left: Unparent selected object(s) (Move Out).\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\par
Menu equivalents are available under {\i Tools} > {\i Hierarchy Navigator}: Move Up, Move Down, Move Out (Unparent), and Move In (Parent to Above).\par
\pard\sa200\par
\pard\b\fs22 5.2 Project Move Mode\b0\par
Move Mode lets you move assets between folders using only the keyboard. Enter Move Mode with assets selected in the Project window, browse to a target folder, and confirm.\par
\pard\li360\sa120\sl276\slmult1
Step 1. Select one or more assets in the Project window.\par
Step 2. Press Ctrl+Shift+Up or Ctrl+Shift+Down to enter Move Mode. A green outline highlights the current target folder.\par
Step 3. Press Up or Down to browse sibling folders at the same level.\par
Step 4. Press Right to enter the highlighted folder and browse its children.\par
Step 5. Press Left to go up one level.\par
Step 6. Press Enter to move the selected assets into the highlighted folder.\par
Step 7. Press Esc or click anywhere else to cancel Move Mode.\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\par
Notes:\par
\pard\li360\sa120\sl276\slmult1
{\pntext\f1\'b7} File moves are file operations and are not covered by Unity Undo.\par
{\pntext\f1\'b7} Name conflicts are resolved automatically with a unique name.\par
{\pntext\f1\'b7} Moving a folder into itself is prevented.\par
\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
\pard\b\fs22 5.3 Settings and Help Window\b0\par
Open the window from {\i Tools} > {\i Hierarchy Navigator} > {\i Settings && Help}. The window lists every shortcut, explains the Move Mode workflow, and provides usage tips.\par
\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
\pard\b\fs24 6. Script Reference\b0\par
Editor Navigator requires no scripting by the user. All functionality is driven by menu commands and keyboard shortcuts, so there is no public API you need to call.\par
For developers who want to extend or integrate the tool, the source code is organised in the {\i HierarchyNavigator} namespace and compiled only in the Unity Editor (it is not included in player builds):\par
\pard\li360\sa120\sl276\slmult1
{\pntext\f1\'b7} {\b HierarchyNavigatorTool} (static class): Hierarchy move, parent, and unparent logic, including the registered shortcuts.\par
{\pntext\f1\'b7} {\b ProjectNavigatorTool} (static class): Project Move Mode logic and Project window rendering callbacks.\par
{\pntext\f1\'b7} {\b HierarchyNavigatorSettings} (EditorWindow): the Settings and Help window.\par
\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
\pard\b\fs24 7. Troubleshooting\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa120\sl276\slmult1
{\pntext\f1\'b7} Shortcuts do nothing: make sure the correct window is focused (Hierarchy for Hierarchy shortcuts, Project for Move Mode), and check for shortcut conflicts in Edit > Shortcuts.\par
{\pntext\f1\'b7} No folder highlight appears in Move Mode: the highlight is drawn in the Project window list view; switch to a list or two-column layout if you are in one-column mode.\par
{\pntext\f1\'b7} Menu items are missing: wait for the import to finish, then refresh the project with Assets > Refresh and recompile.\par
\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
